  "validity_conditions": [
    "Validated for models whose aggregate and capability scores fall inside the calibrated ranges of the nine-model pool (validity_range.calibrated_score_ranges). Outside them the estimate is an extrapolation: held-out error roughly doubles to quadruples per dimension; confirm on the full benchmark.",
    "Item parameters assume the v1 ordinal grading map; any change to the grading map requires revalidation.",
    "Pseudo-respondents stabilise item parameters but are variants of the nine models, not independent ability points.",
    "The subset is not a substitute for full evaluation when a new capability dimension is introduced."
  ],
  "usage": [
    "Designed for RANKING models and recovering CAPABILITY PROFILES.",
    "Score levels: use the calibrated estimator (aggregate: blend; capability: calibrated per-dimension); the naive subset mean is biased on this subset (safety naive MAE ~13 pp).",
    "Capability rankings: use the naive per-dimension subset means.",
    "If only aggregate score LEVELS are needed, a uniform random subset of equal size is at least as accurate."
  ],
  "responsible_use": "Report subset-based scores as estimates with the LOMO interval, disclose the subset version and size, and state whether the model lies inside the validated range."
